<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow">About Thandeka</div><h1>A legal practice grounded in rights, dignity and accountability.</h1><p class="lead">A human rights lawyer and researcher whose work centres on environmental justice, public-interest law and the rights of communities affected by inequality and harmful decisions.</p></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="container content-grid"><div class="prose"><h2>Biography</h2><p>Thandeka Kathi is a South African attorney and human rights specialist with experience in legal research, litigation, policy advocacy and public-interest work. Her areas of expertise include public and constitutional law, housing, water, prospecting and mining, and environmental law.</p><p>She serves as Programme Head: Pollution and Climate Change at the Centre for Environmental Rights. Her work includes legal advocacy and strategic litigation aimed at addressing air pollution and climate change, strengthening environmental protections, and holding emitters and state decision-makers accountable.</p><p>Before joining the Centre for Environmental Rights, she worked at the Centre for Applied Legal Studies at the University of the Witwatersrand, including in a leadership role focused on home, land and rural democracy. Her broader career has included research at the Social Justice Coalition, work connected to the Constitutional Court of South Africa, and legal practice.</p><p>Her public-interest approach reflects a commitment to ensuring that people and communities whose rights are overlooked can participate in decisions affecting their lives, homes, health and environment.</p><div class="notice">Please have Thandeka review and approve this biography and career timeline before publication.</div></div><aside class="sidebar-panel"><h3>Professional profile</h3><ul><li>Human rights and public-interest law</li><li>Environmental and climate justice</li><li>Strategic litigation and legal advocacy</li><li>Research and policy development</li><li>Community and socio-economic rights</li></ul><p><a class="text-link" href="https://cer.org.za/team/thandeka-kathi" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Official institutional biography</a></p></aside></div></section>
